(Hyun Moo is proud of himself for taking on a new challenge.)

267
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,600
(The first meal in Vietnam, featuring frog)

268
00:13:16,370 --> 00:13:18,740
(First encounter with the braised frog)

269
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,410
Gosh, the leg is...

270
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:28,550
(Dear Moo Friends, is frog going too far?)

271
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,750
(Hyun Moo is agonized.)

272
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:35,390
(It's good. Why isn't he eating it?)

273
00:13:43,890 --> 00:13:45,200
(Intimidated)

274
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,560
(Intimidated again)

275
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:50,800
(He's finally eating it.)

276
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:04,980
It's good.

277
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:09,720
It actually tastes like chicken.

278
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:12,160
It's the thigh. Yes!

279
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:19,030
(He’s discovered just how tasty frog can be.)

280
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:21,800
The thigh meat is good.

281
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,800
It's the shape of the frog that makes it tough.

282
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:29,440
It tastes perfectly good. It doesn't have any unpleasant smell.

283
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:34,280
(He slowly immerses in the local culture.)

284
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:37,979
Frog is all right.

285
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,420
This is my first frog.

286
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:44,490
(Summer of 2026, he tastes his first-ever frog.)

287
00:14:47,690 --> 00:14:49,030
The beer is great.

288
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,769
(It's an unfamiliar place...)

289
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:58,540
(he randomly discovered.)

290
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:06,310
(Travel always puts the mind at ease.)

291
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:14,949
So these are the noodles.

292
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:16,150
Am I supposed to dip it in the sauce?

293
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:18,919
Is it like tsukemen?

294
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:19,960
(Is it eaten like tsukemen?)

295
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:22,760
(Checking other people)

296
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:24,759
(Hyun Moo looks around,)

297
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:27,530
(but he's the only one who ordered noodles.)

298
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,169
(He chucks them into the sauce.)

299
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:30,400
Is this the right way?

300
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:35,140
(Anxious)

301
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:36,970
Excuse me.

302
00:15:37,910 --> 00:15:38,980
Hello.

303
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:42,249
Is this the right way of eating?

304
00:15:42,250 --> 00:15:43,980
- This is my first time.
- Yes.

305
00:15:45,350 --> 00:15:47,179
- Do I put the noodles in here?
- Okay.

306
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:48,450
Right?

307
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:50,950
- Well...
- Yes?

308
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:54,289
Put the noodles inside.

309
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:56,030
Put the noodles inside? Here?

310
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:58,499
- Mix the...
- Mix them and eat?

311
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,500
Yes.

312
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,880
(The beloved local delicacy: Braised frog and noodles)

313
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,949
Do you like this dish?

314
00:16:14,950 --> 00:16:16,279
- Yes, I like it.
- Frog?

315
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,550
(He sits down.)

316
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,949
This food is very delicious.

317
00:16:20,950 --> 00:16:23,150
- Delicious?
- Delicious.

318
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:26,719
I usually come here.

319
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,960
- With your family.
- With my family.

320
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:32,259
You come here and...

321
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,899
You don't eat chicken or beef. You only eat frog?

322
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:36,229
- Yes.
- Really?

323
00:16:36,230 --> 00:16:37,330
I see.

324
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,040
- Okay.
- Okay.

325
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,969
He is sitting too close.

326
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:43,039
- Nice to meet you.
- Okay. Thank you.

327
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,909
(People in Da Nang are very kind.)

328
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:45,910
Oh?

329
00:16:45,911 --> 00:16:47,139
What is that?

330
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:49,180
This is my family.

331
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:50,950
No, I mean...

332
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:55,349
It's fried rice with frog.

333
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:57,049
It's called com chay in Vietnamese.

334
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:58,589
- Com chay?
- Com chay?

335
00:16:58,590 --> 00:16:59,890
Com chay.

336
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:05,830
(The frog dish can be enjoyed in a variety of ways.)

337
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:10,270
(Scorched rice and braise frog is a dish with a nice crunch.)

338
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:14,970
(Hot porridge and braised frog is the popular restorative dish.)

339
00:17:15,420 --> 00:17:19,890
(Thick noodles and braised frog is a filling meal.)

340
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:24,680
(The Vietnamese enjoy frog in many ways.)

341
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:26,820
Okay. Thank you.

342
00:17:26,850 --> 00:17:28,750
You're welcome.

343
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:31,490
So this is the right way to eat it.

344
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:43,170
It tastes quite good.

345
00:17:46,570 --> 00:17:47,809
I've never eaten something like this before.

346
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:49,150
(Hyun Moo seems to like it.)

347
00:17:57,890 --> 00:17:59,020
This is my first time to eat something like this.

348
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:02,350
It's my first time eating braised meat in Vietnam.

349
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:07,860
This is tasty.

350
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:10,560
You're a naughty boy, aren't you?

351
00:18:11,910 --> 00:18:14,800
(He's got a mischievous little frog face.)

352
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:18,410
(He's been running around, not eating.)

353
00:18:18,650 --> 00:18:21,040
(It looks good, doesn't it? Here.)

354
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:23,510
(I don't want to eat.)

355
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:25,810
(I'm going to play!)

356
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:28,080
(Gosh, this boy.)

357
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:32,479
(Every child in the world...)

358
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,720
(wants to play and not eat.)

359
00:18:35,050 --> 00:18:36,660
(Acting cute)

360
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:41,090
He's a good dad.

361
00:18:42,490 --> 00:18:44,060
That's why he's married.

362
00:18:44,530 --> 00:18:45,800
He's a good man.

363
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:50,170
(Dad, have some water.)

364
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:53,299
(Big uncle's smile)

365
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:56,009
(Give me the delivery charge.)

366
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,670
(Here you go.)

367
00:18:58,340 --> 00:18:59,709
I will give you some too. Here.

368
00:18:59,710 --> 00:19:01,080
(Here)

369
00:19:02,510 --> 00:19:03,550
Okay.

370
00:19:04,450 --> 00:19:05,580
So kind.

371
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,820
I should go now.

372
00:19:10,490 --> 00:19:11,959
- How much is it?
- It's 3.5 dollars.

373
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,960
- It's 3.5.
- It's 3.5.

374
00:19:14,090 --> 00:19:15,090
Yes.

375
00:19:15,091 --> 00:19:17,590
If I remove zero from it, that becomes...

376
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:19,199
Is it just 3.5 dollars?

377
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,300
(He paid 3.5 dollars for braised pork, noodles, and beer.)

378
00:19:21,470 --> 00:19:22,669
Here.

379
00:19:22,670 --> 00:19:25,499
(The big uncle returns the favour.)

380
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:26,540
Thank you.

381
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:28,510
Bye.

382
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,840
Thank you. Bye.

383
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,540
You won't remember this day.

384
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,580
Bye, you.

385
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,020
Gosh, I'm full.

386
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:47,219
(It was my first time trying frog, but it tasted nice and familiar.)

387
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:50,030
(Next time, I will make sure to try the frog porridge.)

388
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:54,799
I booked a hotel, so I should head there now.

389
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:55,910
The time is...

390
00:19:57,330 --> 00:19:59,540
It's already past midnight here.

391
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:02,650
It's 2am in Korea.

392
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:04,919
Look at the night market.

393
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,809
When do these night markets close?

394
00:20:06,810 --> 00:20:09,010
(The night streets of Da Nang are still brightly lit.)

395
00:20:11,050 --> 00:20:12,249
Should I drop by?

396
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:13,949
(The locals make him drop by.)

397
00:20:13,950 --> 00:20:15,990
Right. This is the vibe I wanted.

398
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:20,620
(People enjoy the night at the brightly lit streets.)

399
00:20:22,330 --> 00:20:24,229
Yes, I wanted this bustling vibe.

400
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:26,059
(He trusts his instinct and gets off the car.)

401
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:27,670
Oh, yes. I love it.

402
00:20:28,930 --> 00:20:31,909
(Are there any Koreans?)

403
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:32,970
Fried rice.

404
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,410
(Locals)

405
00:20:34,970 --> 00:20:37,210
(Locals)

406
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:39,150
It's nice.

407
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,389
There are no Koreans.

408
00:20:42,390 --> 00:20:43,660
(He found the local night market with no Korean tourists.)

409
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:45,179
(Groaning)

410
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:46,220
Goodness.

411
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:48,690
Gosh, it's killing me.

412
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,719
(The Taxi Driver's Restaurant Recommendation)

413
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:55,589
(Night Market)

414
00:20:55,590 --> 00:20:57,530
I should eat something with broth.

415
00:20:58,030 --> 00:20:59,829
(Looking)

416
00:20:59,830 --> 00:21:01,570
(Around)

417
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:09,710
(Nobody recognises Hyun Moo.)

418
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,420
Are they not going to give me the menu? Here it is.

419
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,680
It's all written in Vietnamese.

420
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:23,690
(Blue paper and black writings are what he sees.)

421
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:27,169
This shows that Koreans don't come here.

422
00:21:27,170 --> 00:21:28,359
(There's no English either on the menu.)

423
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,400
There's no English on the menu.

424
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:34,170
(He ends up using the translating app.)

425
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:36,069
(Translated)

426
00:21:36,070 --> 00:21:39,739
"The name of this place is 'Fat Hyo Sung.'"

427
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:40,740
(The name of the place is Fat Hyo Sung.)

428
00:21:40,741 --> 00:21:42,440
The first dishes on the menu are sweet and sour pork,

429
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,680
false, frog chicken wing...

430
00:21:46,310 --> 00:21:47,480
What does this mean?

431
00:21:47,650 --> 00:21:50,780
(The translation quality is poor.)

432
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:52,480
- Do you have the English menu?
- No.

433
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:54,079
(I see.)

434
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,890
(He picks up the translating app again.)

435
00:21:57,390 --> 00:21:58,420
Okay?

436
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,090
(Do you have the pho with broth?)

437
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:04,230
Quán không có bán phở

438
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:06,760
"I don't sell it."

439
00:22:08,930 --> 00:22:10,029
No pho.

440
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:11,369
(We don't have pho.)

441
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:12,370
Okay.

442
00:22:12,371 --> 00:22:15,310
What's the bestselling dish?

443
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:18,340
Xiên nướng.

444
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:22,009
Skewers.

445
00:22:22,010 --> 00:22:25,320
(Char-grilled skewers)

446
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:29,390
(Everyone is holding a skewer.)

447
00:22:29,950 --> 00:22:31,519
Why is nobody selling pho?

448
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,890
(It's hard to eat pho.)

449
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:37,830
Okay. Tiger beer.

450
00:22:38,330 --> 00:22:39,400
Gosh, it's lukewarm.

451
00:22:40,430 --> 00:22:42,170
Okay. I got ice.

452
00:22:43,130 --> 00:22:44,199
Ice.

453
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,170
(The room temperature beer is served with ice.)

454
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:49,309
(Ice and beer)

455
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:53,610
(200% refreshed.)

456
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:59,280
(Enjoying the night breeze, he relaxedly sips the beer.)

457
00:23:00,820 --> 00:23:01,950
It's fascinating.

458
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:06,120
They bring their kids. They are very family-oriented.

459
00:23:07,860 --> 00:23:10,029
They could leave the kids home...

460
00:23:10,030 --> 00:23:12,300
and come out by themselves.

461
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:14,769
They are here together, enjoying the night snacks.

462
00:23:14,770 --> 00:23:17,269
(They enjoy the night outing with the family.)

463
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,700
And the dads are all young.

464
00:23:20,670 --> 00:23:24,510
(Feeling sad)

465
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:32,549
(We must be willing to let go of the life we planned...)

466
00:23:32,550 --> 00:23:35,689
(in order to make room for the real life...)

467
00:23:35,690 --> 00:23:37,320
(awaiting us.)

468
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:52,039
(The char-grilled skewers are served.)

469
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,040
Thank you.

470
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:56,040
(Satisfied)

471
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:57,740
It will go perfectly with beer.

472
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,179
(Dear Moo Friends, can you smell the aroma?)

473
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,509
(I want to go!)

474
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:02,580
It smells smoky.

475
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:11,219
It tastes smoky. It's got that char-grilled smell.

476
00:24:11,220 --> 00:24:12,459
(The juicy chicken is infused with the smoky aroma.)

477
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:13,560
It's nicely sweet.

478
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,330
It pairs perfectly with beer.

479
00:24:26,370 --> 00:24:27,540
When it comes to Vietnam,

480
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:30,470
street food beats hotel room service.

481
00:24:39,050 --> 00:24:40,120
Hello?

482
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:42,850
- Hyun Moo.
- Are you coming?

483
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:45,490
I just landed.

484
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:47,020
Where are you?

485
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,690
I just landed at the airport.

486
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:51,289
Where should we go?

487
00:24:51,290 --> 00:24:53,360
I will send you the address.

488
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:55,569
Call a taxi on Grab...

489
00:24:55,570 --> 00:24:56,830
and ask the driver to come here.

490
00:24:57,530 --> 00:24:58,670
- Okay.
- Bye.

491
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,340
I wouldn't let my buddy...

492
00:25:02,970 --> 00:25:04,470
eat just anything.

493
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:06,209
Excuse me.

494
00:25:06,210 --> 00:25:07,880
(Additional order!)

495
00:25:08,810 --> 00:25:11,009
(He orders fried bitter melon and egg and beef tendon stir-fry...)

496
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:14,019
(for his mysterious friend.)

497
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:15,050
Okay.

498
00:25:15,620 --> 00:25:18,860
(Who's coming to meet Hyun Moo?)

499
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:20,520
When I was a broadcaster,

500
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,030
he was a regular guest to "Star Golden Bell."

501
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:25,729
He's popular, good-looking,

502
00:25:25,730 --> 00:25:27,300
a great dancer and singer,

503
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:30,100
and he's goofy.

504
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:32,170
(Several hours ago at Incheon International Airport)

505
00:25:32,900 --> 00:25:34,099
I'm a minimalist,

506
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:35,740
so I don't like packing a lot.

507
00:25:36,710 --> 00:25:38,580
(Minimal travel buddy, Lee Joon)

508
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:41,849
There's this excitement you feel before you fly.

509
00:25:41,850 --> 00:25:43,210
It's the airport smell.

510
00:25:44,210 --> 00:25:46,049
I feel like a star.

511
00:25:46,050 --> 00:25:47,320
(I feel like a star.)

512
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:48,520
(The day of Lee Joon's pre-show interview)

513
00:25:48,521 --> 00:25:49,619
What's this show all about?

514
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:50,620
(3 days before the shoot)

515
00:25:50,890 --> 00:25:52,960
(What's Lee Joon's travel style?)

516
00:25:53,190 --> 00:25:55,630
I often travel virtually.

517
00:25:56,230 --> 00:25:57,829
I normally plan my days.

518
00:25:57,830 --> 00:26:00,129
But the only time I don't plan...

519
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:01,670
is when I travel.

520
00:26:02,130 --> 00:26:05,470
When I travel with my friends or my partner,

521
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:07,440
we often get into an argument.

522
00:26:07,970 --> 00:26:10,670
So I am a little traumatized about travelling.

523
00:26:11,170 --> 00:26:12,409
I have mild PTSD.

524
00:26:12,410 --> 00:26:14,810
So if I were to travel,

525
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,210
I want my travel companion to be happy.

526
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:18,620
That's the most important thing.

527
00:26:19,050 --> 00:26:20,380
I want to...

528
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:23,489
experience the local culture...

529
00:26:23,490 --> 00:26:25,120
and learn about the country.

530
00:26:25,460 --> 00:26:27,360
The more local it is, the more fun it is.

531
00:26:28,190 --> 00:26:30,260
I want a memorable trip.

532
00:26:32,630 --> 00:26:35,770
(Hyun Moo's travel buddy, Lee Joon appears.)

533
00:26:36,030 --> 00:26:37,230
I don't see him. Where is he?

534
00:26:38,370 --> 00:26:40,140
(He spots Hyun Moo.)

535
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:42,940
(Hyun Moo spots him too.)

536
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:46,809
(Just looking at each other makes them burst out laughing.)

537
00:26:46,810 --> 00:26:48,850
It's strange to see you here.

538
00:26:48,980 --> 00:26:50,550
Don't I look like a middle-aged Vietnamese man?

539
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:53,180
- Have a seat.
- You blend in perfectly.

