1422
01:02:27,620 --> 01:02:29,519
You may think it's a crowded place,

1423
01:02:29,520 --> 01:02:31,150
but they're all Vietnamese people.

1424
01:02:31,750 --> 01:02:33,220
You don't find a single Korean.

1425
01:02:35,090 --> 01:02:36,189
There's no Korean.

1426
01:02:36,190 --> 01:02:37,559
- There's a monkey.
- What?

1427
01:02:37,560 --> 01:02:38,690
There's a monkey.

1428
01:02:38,990 --> 01:02:40,060
What?

1429
01:02:40,360 --> 01:02:42,030
- It looks like a baby.
- A baby?

1430
01:02:42,730 --> 01:02:43,869
- Where did it go?
- Right here. Goodness.

1431
01:02:43,870 --> 01:02:44,970
What are they doing?

1432
01:02:45,870 --> 01:02:48,070
Goodness.

1433
01:02:48,370 --> 01:02:50,440
- This one looks like the leader.
- Yes.

1434
01:02:51,070 --> 01:02:52,609
- There's a baby.
- A baby?

1435
01:02:52,610 --> 01:02:54,280
- It's a baby.
- The one at the back.

1436
01:02:55,780 --> 01:02:56,910
I guess they're a family.

1437
01:02:58,180 --> 01:03:02,850
(Monkeys welcome you Bán Đảo Sơn Trà.)

1438
01:03:03,380 --> 01:03:04,550
I've never seen them from this close.

1439
01:03:04,820 --> 01:03:06,790
What is this? Is this a zoo?

1440
01:03:07,160 --> 01:03:10,119
The baby.

1441
01:03:10,120 --> 01:03:11,330
(Moving)

1442
01:03:11,590 --> 01:03:13,900
Goodness. What is he doing?

1443
01:03:14,200 --> 01:03:15,899
(Getting startled)

1444
01:03:15,900 --> 01:03:17,629
He's worried we might hurt his baby.

1445
01:03:17,630 --> 01:03:19,129
That's cool.

1446
01:03:19,130 --> 01:03:21,400
He's trying to guard his baby.

1447
01:03:22,100 --> 01:03:23,439
I really love the eyes.

1448
01:03:23,440 --> 01:03:25,969
They're saying, "I'll protect my family."

1449
01:03:25,970 --> 01:03:27,210
(I'll protect my family!)

1450
01:03:28,910 --> 01:03:30,410
I wonder if we'll see many of them at the beach.

1451
01:03:31,510 --> 01:03:33,450
We have to look for the yellow tree.

1452
01:03:33,710 --> 01:03:35,579
The one painted in yellow?

1453
01:03:35,580 --> 01:03:36,580
Yes.

1454
01:03:36,581 --> 01:03:38,320
(Where would the yellow tree be?)

1455
01:03:43,820 --> 01:03:46,330
It's like we've entered a jungle.

1456
01:03:46,960 --> 01:03:48,629
There aren't any Koreans here.

1457
01:03:48,630 --> 01:03:49,700
Right.

1458
01:03:52,100 --> 01:03:53,269
This is interesting.

1459
01:03:53,270 --> 01:03:58,110
(There isn't a single Korean among all these people.)

1460
01:03:59,910 --> 01:04:02,839
- It's over there!
- What's there?

1461
01:04:02,840 --> 01:04:04,010
- The tree.
- It's over there!

1462
01:04:06,110 --> 01:04:07,920
This is it.

1463
01:04:08,820 --> 01:04:10,550
You need to look for this tree.

1464
01:04:12,450 --> 01:04:14,390
How is it at the center?

1465
01:04:14,760 --> 01:04:17,019
Look for a beach with no Koreans.

1466
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:18,129
Bãi Da.

1467
01:04:18,130 --> 01:04:20,190
(Bãi Da)

1468
01:04:20,700 --> 01:04:24,870
(As they walk along the long, winding path)

1469
01:04:25,430 --> 01:04:27,170
Look at the entrance.

1470
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:30,240
Who would know about this among tourists here?

1471
01:04:31,310 --> 01:04:32,410
It's amazing.

1472
01:04:33,510 --> 01:04:35,779
It's nice because it looks like untouched nature.

1473
01:04:35,780 --> 01:04:36,879
Right.

1474
01:04:36,880 --> 01:04:37,950
It looks natural.

1475
01:04:38,110 --> 01:04:39,209
(Screaming)

1476
01:04:39,210 --> 01:04:41,250
(Screaming)

1477
01:04:42,050 --> 01:04:44,549
(They can hear excited squeals from a distance.)

1478
01:04:44,550 --> 01:04:46,190
It's the sound of the locals.

1479
01:04:46,590 --> 01:04:48,320
I can see the beach!

1480
01:04:51,960 --> 01:04:53,389
There are quite a few people here.

1481
01:04:53,390 --> 01:04:54,530
The locals.

1482
01:04:56,000 --> 01:04:57,030
What?

1483
01:05:00,270 --> 01:05:02,940
Yes. Nice view.

1484
01:05:03,070 --> 01:05:04,869
No wonder there aren't many people.

1485
01:05:04,870 --> 01:05:06,709
- How would people know this place?
- They wouldn't.

1486
01:05:06,710 --> 01:05:08,080
How would they come here?

1487
01:05:08,180 --> 01:05:09,479
They really wouldn't know.

1488
01:05:09,480 --> 01:05:10,809
(Bai Da Beach, Da Nang's hidden gem)

1489
01:05:10,810 --> 01:05:12,110
Bai Da.

1490
01:05:12,210 --> 01:05:13,479
They really wouldn't know.

1491
01:05:13,480 --> 01:05:14,849
(Bai Da Beach, Da Nang's hidden gem)

1492
01:05:14,850 --> 01:05:16,120
Bai Da.

1493
01:05:17,290 --> 01:05:19,850
It's like a private beach.

1494
01:05:21,990 --> 01:05:24,860
(Instead of the landmark everyone visits...)

1495
01:05:26,430 --> 01:05:29,300
(They came to a real local spot only locals know of.)

1496
01:05:29,900 --> 01:05:30,900
(This is fun!)

1497
01:05:30,901 --> 01:05:33,469
It's just like how we went to the beach when we were young.

1498
01:05:33,470 --> 01:05:34,740
(Bai Da Beach, Da Nang's hidden gem)

1499
01:05:37,810 --> 01:05:41,780
(Da Nang locals relaxing by the calm sea)

1500
01:05:43,640 --> 01:05:46,209
Look over there.

1501
01:05:46,210 --> 01:05:48,220
- Right. It's a wedding photo shoot.
- Wedding...

1502
01:05:48,720 --> 01:05:49,720
A wedding photo shoot.

1503
01:05:49,721 --> 01:05:50,749
(It's a famous spot for wedding photo shoots.)

1504
01:05:50,750 --> 01:05:51,819
(This is Hyunmoo Road)

1505
01:05:51,820 --> 01:05:53,390
We're not going to My Khe Beach.

1506
01:05:53,420 --> 01:05:55,059
- We're going to Bai Da Beach.
- Bai Da Beach.

1507
01:05:55,060 --> 01:05:56,660
(Bai Da Beach)

1508
01:05:58,360 --> 01:06:00,460
They're all Vietnamese.

1509
01:06:00,830 --> 01:06:03,560
It's a Vietnamese vacation spot.

1510
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:08,300
It's a vacation spot for families.

1511
01:06:09,500 --> 01:06:11,109
(If you're tired of the busy sightseeing,)

1512
01:06:11,110 --> 01:06:12,710
(head to Bai Da Beach for a quiet rest.)

1513
01:06:13,040 --> 01:06:15,210
That looks like fun.

1514
01:06:15,510 --> 01:06:17,949
- They're riding pedal boats.
- Yes.

1515
01:06:17,950 --> 01:06:21,080
There's a banana boat that's going over there.

1516
01:06:21,580 --> 01:06:22,979
They all look like fun.

1517
01:06:22,980 --> 01:06:24,190
- Do you like them all?
- Yes.

1518
01:06:24,590 --> 01:06:26,989
I think...

1519
01:06:26,990 --> 01:06:29,389
if we talk to the place that looks like the headquarters,

1520
01:06:29,390 --> 01:06:31,089
we can decide what activities we want to do.

1521
01:06:31,090 --> 01:06:33,229
We can decide the spot we'll use too.

1522
01:06:33,230 --> 01:06:36,960
(The vacationers have settled between the rocks.)

1523
01:06:37,200 --> 01:06:39,029
This looks like the best spot.

1524
01:06:39,030 --> 01:06:40,369
- This spot is nice.
- Right here.

1525
01:06:40,370 --> 01:06:41,439
It looks expensive.

1526
01:06:41,440 --> 01:06:42,799
It might not be that expensive.

1527
01:06:42,800 --> 01:06:45,470
(Hyun Moo wants this spot.)

1528
01:06:45,810 --> 01:06:47,510
- Xin chào.
- Hello. Xin chào.

1529
01:06:48,640 --> 01:06:49,839
(Do you want to take that spot?)

1530
01:06:49,840 --> 01:06:51,450
- How much is it?
- How much is it?

1531
01:06:51,550 --> 01:06:52,550
Hai Trăm dong.

1532
01:06:54,280 --> 01:06:55,619
- Two hundred thousand.
- Two hundred thousand.

1533
01:06:55,620 --> 01:06:56,849
How much is 200,000 dong?

1534
01:06:56,850 --> 01:06:58,689
It's about 10 dollars.

1535
01:06:58,690 --> 01:07:00,149
That's quite nice.

1536
01:07:00,150 --> 01:07:01,560
(Until sunset)

1537
01:07:01,660 --> 01:07:03,089
All day?

1538
01:07:03,090 --> 01:07:04,530
(For 10 dollars, they can enjoy the prime beach spot all day.)

1539
01:07:08,200 --> 01:07:09,459
What about this?

1540
01:07:09,460 --> 01:07:11,500
- All inclusive.
- All inclusive.

1541
01:07:15,000 --> 01:07:16,039
Free?

1542
01:07:16,040 --> 01:07:17,200
(Getting flustered)

1543
01:07:17,540 --> 01:07:18,640
Ba trăm một người.

1544
01:07:19,310 --> 01:07:20,539
It's 300,000 dong per person.

1545
01:07:20,540 --> 01:07:22,510
Then that's 15 dollars.

1546
01:07:22,680 --> 01:07:23,810
It's 15 dollars.

1547
01:07:24,280 --> 01:07:25,749
- Okay.
- All day.

1548
01:07:25,750 --> 01:07:27,179
Let's go, all-day project!

1549
01:07:27,180 --> 01:07:28,220
(Total: 800,000 dong, which is approximately 40 dollars)

1550
01:07:28,750 --> 01:07:30,990
(Let's go to our prime spot!)

1551
01:07:31,350 --> 01:07:33,190
Yes!

1552
01:07:34,460 --> 01:07:36,589
How is this best spot empty?

1553
01:07:36,590 --> 01:07:37,760
(Hyun Moo can't believe this luck.)

1554
01:07:38,330 --> 01:07:40,060
- This is nice.
- Yes.

1555
01:07:42,260 --> 01:07:43,929
(Lying down)

1556
01:07:43,930 --> 01:07:45,170
This is so nice.

1557
01:07:45,800 --> 01:07:47,070
This is so nice.

1558
01:07:48,170 --> 01:07:49,339
This is what I've been dreaming about.

1559
01:07:49,340 --> 01:07:51,510
(The perfect rest Hyun Moo dreamed of)

1560
01:07:51,970 --> 01:07:54,340
How do Koreans not know this place?

1561
01:07:55,580 --> 01:07:57,209
We have to go barefoot...

1562
01:07:57,210 --> 01:07:58,379
from here.

1563
01:07:58,380 --> 01:07:59,649
Of course.

1564
01:07:59,650 --> 01:08:01,620
We should go barefoot. This is a luxury.

1565
01:08:03,350 --> 01:08:04,490
I'll remove them.

1566
01:08:06,250 --> 01:08:07,690
Should I go down there and have some fun?

1567
01:08:07,860 --> 01:08:08,860
Have fun.

1568
01:08:09,620 --> 01:08:11,929
You can do the activities when you want to.

1569
01:08:11,930 --> 01:08:13,259
Really?

1570
01:08:13,260 --> 01:08:16,400
It looked like you had to wear life jackets.

1571
01:08:17,260 --> 01:08:19,430
(He wore it.)

1572
01:08:20,000 --> 01:08:21,610
It's raining.

1573
01:08:22,650 --> 01:08:25,070
(It was hot all day long.)

1574
01:08:25,940 --> 01:08:29,440
(Vietnam's heat just wouldn't let up.)

1575
01:08:30,740 --> 01:08:33,820
(A welcome rain to cool things down)

1576
01:08:34,080 --> 01:08:36,080
The rain feels so nice.

1577
01:08:37,360 --> 01:08:40,620
(Even a rainy beach is a playground for them.)

1578
01:08:43,990 --> 01:08:47,800
(Joon is just happy about the cool rain.)

1579
01:08:48,610 --> 01:08:50,900
(Feeling refreshed)

1580
01:08:52,230 --> 01:08:53,630
I don't have extra clothes.

1581
01:08:56,200 --> 01:08:57,910
I'm going shirtless for the first time in a while.

1582
01:08:59,040 --> 01:09:00,320
What am I going to do about the maesaengi?

1583
01:09:01,840 --> 01:09:04,680
(Sealing the maesaengi)

1584
01:09:05,280 --> 01:09:09,650
(The path to the beach seems a bit rough.)

1585
01:09:09,880 --> 01:09:11,489
If you take off your shoes from there...

1586
01:09:11,490 --> 01:09:12,490
(Trying not to laugh)

1587
01:09:12,820 --> 01:09:13,899
It would hurt.

1588
01:09:13,900 --> 01:09:15,360
I should have worn my slippers.

1589
01:09:16,090 --> 01:09:17,190
Shall we go inside?

1590
01:09:19,900 --> 01:09:21,499
- Is it cold?
- The water is cool!

1591
01:09:21,500 --> 01:09:22,930
- Isn't it cold?
- It's perfect.

1592
01:09:23,230 --> 01:09:25,170
- You're lying.
- It's not cold.

1593
01:09:25,470 --> 01:09:26,470
Really.

1594
01:09:26,471 --> 01:09:27,940
You have to enter at once.

1595
01:09:34,380 --> 01:09:36,910
It's so nice!

1596
01:09:41,860 --> 01:09:43,679
- It's too...
- I'm serious.

1597
01:09:43,680 --> 01:09:45,089
It's really okay.

1598
01:09:45,090 --> 01:09:46,490
Trust me. It's really nice.

1599
01:09:47,420 --> 01:09:48,420
(Dipping himself)

1600
01:09:48,690 --> 01:09:49,900
My butt feels cold.

1601
01:09:50,790 --> 01:09:52,259
- It's so nice.
- Stop lying.

1602
01:09:52,260 --> 01:09:53,330
It's so nice.

1603
01:09:54,830 --> 01:09:55,930
My stomach stings.

1604
01:09:58,800 --> 01:10:01,240
(He gets inside in the end.)

1605
01:10:01,700 --> 01:10:05,470
(The water is jade-blue.)

1606
01:10:08,680 --> 01:10:10,949
- It's refreshing.
- It's refreshing.

1607
01:10:10,950 --> 01:10:13,080
You look so cool.

1608
01:10:13,710 --> 01:10:15,380
You look like you're the only one floating in the sea.

1609
01:10:16,620 --> 01:10:19,790
(Let's head out into the open sea!)

1610
01:10:21,620 --> 01:10:23,960
(Having an underwater date)

1611
01:10:28,110 --> 01:10:29,500
(What a sight.)

1612
01:10:29,730 --> 01:10:32,230
They're really having fun.

1613
01:10:35,700 --> 01:10:38,039
How nice. This is nice.

1614
01:10:38,040 --> 01:10:39,109
This is nice.

1615
01:10:39,110 --> 01:10:41,149
There really aren't any Koreans here.

1616
01:10:41,150 --> 01:10:42,280
I feel so much at ease.

1617
01:10:42,610 --> 01:10:43,980
What's with that Gangnam Style?

1618
01:10:44,080 --> 01:10:45,880
(Is that a Korean person?)

1619
01:10:46,210 --> 01:10:48,280
(Does this place not meet the Hyunmoo Road standard?)

1620
01:10:48,620 --> 01:10:50,320
- She's not Korean, right?
- She's not.

1621
01:10:51,320 --> 01:10:52,619
Hello.

1622
01:10:52,620 --> 01:10:54,049
- Hello.
- Hello.

1623
01:10:54,050 --> 01:10:56,459
- Korea!
- Korea.

1624
01:10:56,460 --> 01:10:57,789
Are you a family?

1625
01:10:57,790 --> 01:10:59,569
Yes. We're a family.

1626
01:10:59,570 --> 01:11:02,830
We're from Phu Quoc Island.

1627
01:11:04,530 --> 01:11:06,069
- Phu...
- Phu Quoc Island.

1628
01:11:06,070 --> 01:11:07,699
- Bugok Hawaii?
- Ho Chi Minh.

1629
01:11:07,700 --> 01:11:08,700
Ho Chi Minh!

1630
01:11:08,701 --> 01:11:11,670
- Ho Chi Minh.
- Phu Quoc Island.

1631
01:11:12,940 --> 01:11:14,379
I love Ho Chi Minh.

1632
01:11:14,380 --> 01:11:16,079
How long have you been here?

1633
01:11:16,080 --> 01:11:19,680
- This is my second day.
- Second day.

1634
01:11:19,780 --> 01:11:21,219
I speak a little Korean.

1635
01:11:21,220 --> 01:11:22,479
- A little.
- A little.

1636
01:11:22,480 --> 01:11:23,720
Very good.

1637
01:11:24,920 --> 01:11:27,789
This place is mostly visited by the locals.

1638
01:11:27,790 --> 01:11:29,220
You don't find tourists.

1639
01:11:29,820 --> 01:11:33,830
The Bai Da Beach isn't very well known yet.

1640
01:11:34,700 --> 01:11:39,300
(Only Da Nang locals enjoyed such a nice place.)

1641
01:11:40,230 --> 01:11:42,110
It's my first time seeing Koreans here.

1642
01:11:42,370 --> 01:11:43,940
(Welcome!)

1643
01:11:44,470 --> 01:11:46,409
(They became the first Korean visitors to Bai Da Beach.)

1644
01:11:46,410 --> 01:11:47,470
What do you want to do first?

1645
01:11:47,940 --> 01:11:49,380
The paddle boat first.

1646
01:11:50,480 --> 01:11:52,080
(Screaming)

1647
01:11:53,380 --> 01:11:54,420
I...

1648
01:11:55,180 --> 01:11:58,220
(Screaming)

1649
01:12:01,320 --> 01:12:02,459
- This...
- Okay.

1650
01:12:02,460 --> 01:12:03,860
We're not supposed to face each other.

1651
01:12:04,630 --> 01:12:06,329
This is a must-do for couples.

1652
01:12:06,330 --> 01:12:07,330
Right.

1653
01:12:07,460 --> 01:12:11,130
(In between the couples...)

1654
01:12:11,470 --> 01:12:13,429
Everyone here is a couple except us.

1655
01:12:13,430 --> 01:12:14,869
(The only ones showing off their bromance)

1656
01:12:14,870 --> 01:12:16,570
This isn't something for two men.

1657
01:12:17,440 --> 01:12:18,909
Goodness.

1658
01:12:18,910 --> 01:12:21,180
Why did I come here with a man?

1659
01:12:22,010 --> 01:12:23,039
You look cool right now.

1660
01:12:23,040 --> 01:12:24,340
Make sure my belly doesn't show.

1661
01:12:24,610 --> 01:12:27,550
I'll focus on your upper body. Your face...

1662
01:12:28,550 --> 01:12:30,950
(It's still quite fun for two men to enjoy.)

1663
01:12:31,900 --> 01:12:33,900
Can we go farther? Should we go?

1664
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:35,660
I can paddle with power.

1665
01:12:36,090 --> 01:12:39,460
(Paddling with power in the same spot)

1666
01:12:40,830 --> 01:12:42,300
Are we going forward or not?

1667
01:12:43,200 --> 01:12:44,260
Do you want to switch?

1668
01:12:46,970 --> 01:12:49,170
You might get a role in a drifting movie.

1669
01:12:50,170 --> 01:12:51,170
(He starts with strong paddling.)

1670
01:12:51,171 --> 01:12:53,280
That's good paddling. Keep going forward!

1671
01:12:54,410 --> 01:12:56,680
(We set sail!)

1672
01:12:57,780 --> 01:12:59,050
(Captain Moo Sparrow)

1673
01:13:00,080 --> 01:13:01,080
(The muscular sailor, Lee Joon)

1674
01:13:01,420 --> 01:13:04,550
(The Paddleboard Pirates set sail.)

1675
01:13:05,050 --> 01:13:07,860
(Hyun Moo and Joon cleave through the water.)

1676
01:13:08,900 --> 01:13:12,460
(The two pirates' song echoes through Bai Dai Beach.)

1677
01:13:13,130 --> 01:13:16,130
(Let's keep going.)

1678
01:13:17,030 --> 01:13:18,429
(They've come pretty far, thanks to Joon.)

1679
01:13:18,430 --> 01:13:20,000
To the vast sea!

1680
01:13:22,440 --> 01:13:23,609
You look...

1681
01:13:23,610 --> 01:13:25,069
like a guy who's actually cast away.

1682
01:13:25,070 --> 01:13:27,010
("Cast Away by Jun")

1683
01:13:27,320 --> 01:13:29,940
Wilson!

1684
01:13:31,180 --> 01:13:32,679
(They've completely adjusted to Bai Dai Beach.)

1685
01:13:32,680 --> 01:13:34,380
Let's go!

1686
01:13:34,860 --> 01:13:36,249
(Speeding up)

1687
01:13:36,250 --> 01:13:37,450
- It's scary!
- No!

1688
01:13:37,920 --> 01:13:39,030
It's so scary.

1689
01:13:39,530 --> 01:13:41,790
This is way too scary!

1690
01:13:42,160 --> 01:13:44,219
- It's so scary!
- No!

1691
01:13:44,220 --> 01:13:45,429
Let's go that way.

1692
01:13:45,430 --> 01:13:46,689
(Speeding)

1693
01:13:46,690 --> 01:13:47,860
I'm so scared!

1694
01:13:50,460 --> 01:13:52,300
- No!
- That's scary.

1695
01:13:52,400 --> 01:13:53,609
It's faster than I thought.

1696
01:13:53,610 --> 01:13:57,670
(A thrilling ride through the waves)

1697
01:14:03,740 --> 01:14:05,820
(Happy)

1698
01:14:06,380 --> 01:14:07,450
Don't do it!

1699
01:14:08,050 --> 01:14:09,120
I'm scared.

1700
01:14:09,320 --> 01:14:11,860
I've been trained for this in Gangwon Province.

1701
01:14:15,160 --> 01:14:18,190
(Singing the theme song of "Pirates of the Caribbean" again)

1702
01:14:19,730 --> 01:14:21,229
(Diving passionately)

1703
01:14:21,230 --> 01:14:22,259
I'm alive.

1704
01:14:22,260 --> 01:14:23,700
(Diving passionately)

1705
01:14:24,230 --> 01:14:25,330
I'm alive.

1706
01:14:26,370 --> 01:14:28,740
I still live!

1707
01:14:29,370 --> 01:14:32,240
(They're having as much fun as we're having.)

1708
01:14:32,510 --> 01:14:33,970
Joon, there's a shower.

1709
01:14:34,410 --> 01:14:35,539
Let's wash up.

1710
01:14:35,540 --> 01:14:36,880
Yes, it's too salty.

1711
01:14:38,280 --> 01:14:39,410
It's so cold!

1712
01:14:39,950 --> 01:14:40,980
Oh, man.

1713
01:14:42,250 --> 01:14:43,279
It's too cold.

1714
01:14:43,280 --> 01:14:44,280
(Making a fuss)

1715
01:14:44,550 --> 01:14:46,420
(The body of a man who works out and a man who doesn't)

1716
01:14:46,950 --> 01:14:48,460
I look so small next to him.

1717
01:14:48,860 --> 01:14:51,260
(It's not that fancy, but at least we can shower.)

1718
01:14:51,730 --> 01:14:54,860
(The water must be a bit cold.)

1719
01:14:55,800 --> 01:14:58,109
Don't you crave something sweet because it's too salty?

1720
01:14:58,110 --> 01:14:59,130
I do.

1721
01:14:59,470 --> 01:15:00,610
I'd like some fruit.

1722
01:15:02,400 --> 01:15:03,500
That stings.

1723
01:15:05,340 --> 01:15:06,610
I should wear my pyjamas.

1724
01:15:06,820 --> 01:15:07,879
(Pyjamas?)

1725
01:15:07,880 --> 01:15:10,080
I wear this to bed.

1726
01:15:10,380 --> 01:15:12,250
- Is it the same one again?
- It's for bed.

1727
01:15:12,820 --> 01:15:14,110
I can wash it at home.

1728
01:15:14,380 --> 01:15:16,150
What's the difference between pyjamas and outside clothes?

1729
01:15:16,550 --> 01:15:17,750
They're the same once I wash them.

1730
01:15:18,450 --> 01:15:20,250
All done.

1731
01:15:20,720 --> 01:15:22,860
- I'm all refreshed now.
- That's refreshing.

1732
01:15:23,820 --> 01:15:26,190
How long were we out there? It felt long.

1733
01:15:26,260 --> 01:15:27,460
A day goes by fast.

1734
01:15:28,260 --> 01:15:29,299
It's been so long since I last had fun in the water.

1735
01:15:29,300 --> 01:15:30,330
Same here.

1736
01:15:30,530 --> 01:15:32,530
I haven't had that much fun in so long.

1737
01:15:35,070 --> 01:15:39,210
(They hear music from somewhere.)

1738
01:15:39,650 --> 01:15:40,779
It's pretty similar.

1739
01:15:40,780 --> 01:15:43,680
When we go to a place like this in Korea, there's trot music.

1740
01:15:44,040 --> 01:15:45,080
I know, right?

1741
01:15:45,580 --> 01:15:46,819
- It's...
- That was fun.

1742
01:15:46,820 --> 01:15:48,920
how we went on vacation in the 1980s.

1743
01:15:49,980 --> 01:15:51,529
We went to the beach, laid mats,

1744
01:15:51,530 --> 01:15:52,859
and ate watermelons.

1745
01:15:52,860 --> 01:15:54,899
We'd have braised chicken back in the day.

1746
01:15:54,900 --> 01:15:56,400
- Because we could cook as well.
- Exactly.

1747
01:15:56,570 --> 01:15:57,759
We had portable burners, right?

1748
01:15:57,760 --> 01:15:59,570
(And the way they sit together and share delicious food)

1749
01:16:00,070 --> 01:16:01,130
It's the same.

1750
01:16:01,760 --> 01:16:03,199
How are people so similar?

1751
01:16:03,200 --> 01:16:05,110
(The daily lives that go across borders)

1752
01:16:05,630 --> 01:16:06,780
It feels nice.

1753
01:16:08,500 --> 01:16:10,370
Playing in the water does make you hungry.

1754
01:16:12,540 --> 01:16:15,040
(Did you say you were hungry?)

1755
01:16:17,080 --> 01:16:18,859
- Hello.
- Hello.

1756
01:16:18,860 --> 01:16:20,860
(They see a fruit seller who's passing by.)

1757
01:16:22,180 --> 01:16:23,359
What would you like?

1758
01:16:23,360 --> 01:16:24,549
(In Vietnam, street vendors known as "Hang Rong" allow you...)

1759
01:16:24,550 --> 01:16:25,989
(to buy fruit, snacks, and daily necessities...)

1760
01:16:25,990 --> 01:16:27,399
(right on the street.)

1761
01:16:27,400 --> 01:16:29,030
- Sweet?
- Pardon?

1762
01:16:30,490 --> 01:16:31,490
- Is it sweet?
- Sweet?

1763
01:16:31,491 --> 01:16:33,190
It's sweet? Okay.

1764
01:16:34,090 --> 01:16:35,959
- And...
- Mango.

1765
01:16:35,960 --> 01:16:36,960
- Mango?
- Yes.

1766
01:16:36,961 --> 01:16:38,069
That's a mango.

1767
01:16:38,070 --> 01:16:39,230
- Okay.
- Okay.

1768
01:16:39,610 --> 01:16:41,440
- How much is it?
- It's 20,000 dong for 1.

1769
01:16:43,070 --> 01:16:44,470
Thank you.

1770
01:16:46,070 --> 01:16:47,149
Let's see.

1771
01:16:47,150 --> 01:16:48,340
(Crunch)

1772
01:16:48,440 --> 01:16:50,080
This doesn't taste like mango.

1773
01:16:51,210 --> 01:16:52,210
What is it, then?

1774
01:16:52,910 --> 01:16:54,050
This is a mango?

1775
01:16:54,920 --> 01:16:56,750
It tastes like an apple.

1776
01:16:58,090 --> 01:16:59,719
(Frowning)

1777
01:16:59,720 --> 01:17:01,290
- It's sour, isn't it?
- It's not ripe yet.

1778
01:17:01,590 --> 01:17:03,260
It gets soft when it's ripe, right?

1779
01:17:03,460 --> 01:17:05,129
I've never had a mango like this.

1780
01:17:05,130 --> 01:17:06,260
(Green mango is crunchy and sour.)

1781
01:17:06,400 --> 01:17:08,130
I went to Mexico, and I realised...

1782
01:17:09,070 --> 01:17:10,400
people who lived in hot countries...

1783
01:17:10,930 --> 01:17:12,999
dipped sweet fruit in salt.

1784
01:17:13,000 --> 01:17:14,570
- They dip mango in salt?
- Yes.

1785
01:17:14,840 --> 01:17:17,279
When you live in a hot country, you sweat a lot,

1786
01:17:17,280 --> 01:17:18,570
so you need to replenish sodium.

1787
01:17:18,820 --> 01:17:20,609
So, they dip it in salt.

1788
01:17:20,610 --> 01:17:23,480
Apparently, Vietnamese students bring this salt when they go abroad.

1789
01:17:27,680 --> 01:17:28,820
It's salty and sour.

1790
01:17:29,820 --> 01:17:31,860
(He also tries it.)

1791
01:17:33,190 --> 01:17:35,219
(Hyun Moo can't handle pungent taste.)

1792
01:17:35,220 --> 01:17:36,320
It's too salty.

1793
01:17:37,490 --> 01:17:39,159
(Crunching)

1794
01:17:39,160 --> 01:17:40,260
You seem to eat it well.

1795
01:17:40,900 --> 01:17:42,069
It's not that bad.

1796
01:17:42,070 --> 01:17:43,660
It's not as sweet as I expected.

1797
01:17:44,030 --> 01:17:45,030
Right.

1798
01:17:49,700 --> 01:17:50,840
This is sweeter.

1799
01:17:51,670 --> 01:17:52,940
Is this a coconut? What is it?

1800
01:17:53,510 --> 01:17:55,150
Try it. It's way sweeter.

1801
01:17:56,280 --> 01:17:57,410
What's this?

1802
01:18:00,210 --> 01:18:01,359
It's a jackfruit.

1803
01:18:01,360 --> 01:18:02,879
- Oh, this is a jackfruit?
- What?

1804
01:18:02,880 --> 01:18:03,949
(He's never heard of it.)

1805
01:18:03,950 --> 01:18:05,450
- Jackfruit.
- I've never heard of it before.

1806
01:18:05,650 --> 01:18:08,790
(What lies under the rugged skin will surprise you.)

1807
01:18:12,130 --> 01:18:13,189
It's good.

1808
01:18:13,190 --> 01:18:14,929
(Jackfruit is special for its chewiness and sweetness.)

1809
01:18:14,930 --> 01:18:16,800
It's far sweeter and better.

1810
01:18:17,660 --> 01:18:19,870
The fruit vendors must make a lot of money.

1811
01:18:20,330 --> 01:18:21,650
You can't help but crave it after playing in the water.

1812
01:18:21,740 --> 01:18:24,540
We don't get this in Korea,

1813
01:18:24,610 --> 01:18:26,369
- so it's more interesting...
- Right.

1814
01:18:26,370 --> 01:18:27,440
when I eat it here.

1815
01:18:28,820 --> 01:18:30,980
(Lying down)

1816
01:18:31,880 --> 01:18:33,509
- Oh, boy.
- I love it.

1817
01:18:33,510 --> 01:18:35,150
(He's at an age where he just wants to lie down after eating.)

1818
01:18:38,120 --> 01:18:40,860
(Joon also lies down.)

1819
01:18:45,930 --> 01:18:47,289
This is what I call vacation.

1820
01:18:47,290 --> 01:18:49,500
(The finishing touch to a vacation is a nap.)

1821
01:18:50,300 --> 01:18:53,279
(They relax, listening to the waves...)

1822
01:18:53,280 --> 01:18:55,970
(that sound like a lullaby.)

1823
01:18:58,650 --> 01:19:05,180
(The locals have a culture of taking naps to avoid the heat.)

1824
01:19:07,080 --> 01:19:10,980
(They join the locals, facing the sea breeze.)

1825
01:19:17,120 --> 01:19:18,860
(Opening his eyes)

1826
01:19:19,630 --> 01:19:21,360
Why am I so sleepy?

1827
01:19:22,070 --> 01:19:23,860
- Right?
- I dozed off twice.

1828
01:19:24,030 --> 01:19:26,610
(I thought I was dreaming mid-day.)

1829
01:19:26,780 --> 01:19:28,970
I didn't play that hard, even when I was little.

1830
01:19:29,370 --> 01:19:31,469
(He never played pirate, even when he was a child.)

1831
01:19:31,470 --> 01:19:33,070
I don't think I've ever done that.

1832
01:19:33,280 --> 01:19:35,180
But that freedom...

1833
01:19:35,650 --> 01:19:37,649
was something that we desired...

1834
01:19:37,650 --> 01:19:40,780
from a primitive level.

1835
01:19:41,150 --> 01:19:43,149
- We played so childishly.
- We did.

1836
01:19:43,150 --> 01:19:46,720
It brought back memories from high school.

1837
01:19:47,990 --> 01:19:49,860
I felt like a high school student.

1838
01:19:51,190 --> 01:19:53,229
We fell in the water, giggled about it,

1839
01:19:53,230 --> 01:19:54,400
and threw each other into the ocean.

1840
01:19:54,930 --> 01:19:56,029
I felt liberated.

1841
01:19:56,030 --> 01:19:57,360
(It was all the more liberating due to the rain.)

1842
01:19:59,000 --> 01:20:01,839
Although it was childish, it was so much fun.

1843
01:20:01,840 --> 01:20:04,670
It was like I took a nice break with a good friend.

1844
01:20:09,910 --> 01:20:11,579
(Their trip begins now.)

1845
01:20:11,580 --> 01:20:12,980
(Travel itinerary available on our official social media account)

1846
01:20:13,250 --> 01:20:14,920
(Don't come any closer.)

1847
01:20:15,320 --> 01:20:18,150
(I'm so tired.)

1848
01:20:18,400 --> 01:20:20,900
(Panting)

1849
01:20:22,090 --> 01:20:26,260
(A mysterious run in the middle of the night)

1850
01:20:26,490 --> 01:20:29,530
(Screaming)

1851
01:20:29,800 --> 01:20:32,699
(Feeling liberated in a foreign country)

1852
01:20:32,700 --> 01:20:34,200
(I'll be 50 in 2 years.)

1853
01:20:34,830 --> 01:20:37,370
(It tastes better without underwear.)

1854
01:20:37,700 --> 01:20:39,510
That's hot!

1855
01:20:39,670 --> 01:20:40,740
(It's true that you come to Vietnam to eat.)

1856
01:20:42,240 --> 01:20:45,150
(I booked a train.)

1857
01:20:45,480 --> 01:20:46,750
The next station is...

1858
01:20:47,710 --> 01:20:48,750
(Huế)

1859
01:20:52,050 --> 01:20:54,189
(Gyeongju of Vietnam)

1860
01:20:54,190 --> 01:20:56,030
(Where the time of the last dynasty lingers)

1861
01:20:56,820 --> 01:20:58,989
(What looks like a normal train...)

1862
01:20:58,990 --> 01:21:01,330
(holds a surprise inside?)

1863
01:21:01,530 --> 01:21:04,230
- Look at that. That's gorgeous.
- Stunning.

1864
01:21:04,570 --> 01:21:06,170
(What's wrong?)

1865
01:21:06,370 --> 01:21:07,630
(What's going on?)

1866
01:21:08,130 --> 01:21:10,470
(People start heading somewhere.)

1867
01:21:11,650 --> 01:21:14,979
(The two follow them as if they're possessed.)

1868
01:21:14,980 --> 01:21:18,909
(They start dancing at 7am?)

1869
01:21:18,910 --> 01:21:20,749
(Is it a surprise dance-off?)

1870
01:21:20,750 --> 01:21:22,860
(No, they're uniting through dance.)

1871
01:21:23,380 --> 01:21:25,289
(Whatever you expect, it will be better.)

1872
01:21:25,290 --> 01:21:26,950
(An unpredictable road trip)

1873
01:21:28,790 --> 01:21:30,320
We're the only ones on a rickshaw.

1874
01:21:32,438 --> 01:21:33,914
It's really good.

1875
01:21:34,070 --> 01:21:35,039
Really good!
